NymFetcherTest
├── createNymFetcher
│   ├── given a URL that is not a rate API
│   │   ├── it refuses to route it
│   │   └── it never reaches the transport
│   └── given a rate API URL
│       └── it reaches the transport
├── status
│   ├── given nothing has happened yet
│   │   └── it reports disconnected
│   ├── when a watcher subscribes
│   │   ├── it is called immediately with the current status
│   │   └── it is called again on every change
│   ├── when a watcher unsubscribes
│   │   └── it stops being called
│   ├── when the status changes
│   │   ├── it is mirrored to storage for the popup
│   │   └── it is stored under the key the popup reads
│   └── when another context watches the stored status
│       └── it is called on every change
├── on Chrome
│   ├── given no offscreen document exists
│   │   ├── it creates one
│   │   ├── it reports connecting rather than connected
│   │   ├── it asks only about offscreen contexts
│   │   └── it asks for a worker-hosting document at the offscreen page
│   ├── given an offscreen document already exists
│   │   ├── it does not create a second one
│   │   └── it does not ask the platform again
│   ├── given this context already created the document
│   │   └── it reuses it without asking the platform again
│   ├── given the platform cannot report existing contexts
│   │   └── it tries to create one anyway
│   ├── given two fetches race the first creation
│   │   └── it creates exactly one document
│   ├── given the platform reports a document already exists
│   │   ├── it treats the creation as successful
│   │   └── it stops trying to create one
│   ├── given creating the document fails
│   │   ├── it reports an error status
│   │   ├── it rethrows
│   │   └── it names the extension in the console
│   ├── given the fetch succeeds
│   │   ├── it reports connected
│   │   ├── it returns the payload
│   │   └── it defaults a missing status to 200
│   ├── given a second fetch on a live connection
│   │   └── it does not report connecting again
│   ├── given the message channel closes mid-flight
│   │   ├── it forgets the document so the next fetch recreates it
│   │   └── it rethrows as an Error
│   ├── given no response comes back
│   │   └── it forgets the document so the next fetch recreates it
│   ├── given the fetch fails but the transport is fine
│   │   ├── it throws the reported error
│   │   └── it keeps the document
│   ├── given the fetch fails fatally
│   │   ├── it tears the document down
│   │   ├── it reports an error status
│   │   └── it records why the document was torn down
│   ├── destroyNymConnection
│   │   ├── it closes the document
│   │   ├── it reports disconnected
│   │   ├── it forgets the document so the next fetch recreates it
│   │   └── it records the teardown
│   ├── resetNymConnection
│   │   └── it forgets the document without closing it
│   └── resetNymIdentity
│       ├── it closes the document
│       └── it clears the stored identity
└── on Firefox
    ├── given the fetch succeeds
    │   ├── it reports connected
    │   ├── it returns the payload
    │   └── it reports connecting before it reports connected
    ├── given a second fetch on a live connection
    │   └── it does not report connecting again
    ├── given the fetch fails but the transport is fine
    │   ├── it throws the reported error
    │   └── it keeps the client
    ├── given the fetch fails fatally
    │   ├── it destroys the client
    │   ├── it reports an error status
    │   └── it records why the client was destroyed
    ├── given the build flag disagrees with the selected transport
    │   └── it refuses to load the direct client
    ├── given the error carries no message
    │   └── it throws a generic failure
    ├── destroyNymConnection
    │   ├── it reports disconnected
    │   └── it destroys the client
    └── resetNymConnection
        ├── it reports disconnected
        └── it resets the client
